# Bare `krowk` in the full build opens the TUI only when a person is at a
# terminal: stdin and stdout both a TTY. Everywhere else it prints exactly
# what it printed before the TUI existed — except that bare `krowk` piped
# prints the overview rather than the catalog, which takes --json. Any other
# difference is a behaviour change.
krowk
krowk --json
krowk --format human
@stdin hello\n
krowk
@tty krowk
@tty krowk --json
@tty krowk --resume
@tty krowk --model claude-x
